      "Language": "dut",
      "Abstract": {"AbstractText": "A 54-year old man presented with unremitting pain in the left dorsolateral forearm, despite postural advice and glucocorticoid injections. Electromyography and MRI did not show any abnormality. Based on a clinical suspected radial tunnel syndrome, operative decompression was performed."},
